From 96d75170299a927b00782cbc9d73efb96a8ab9cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:33:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a placed create says `chat_link:
 owner_written` only when the owner answers that it wrote the link

PR #2079 review follow-ups (card t_01a1d46503d6ce61):

1. The origin decided `chat_link: owner_written` from the chat id's shape. An owner on core before
   `_link_origin`, or with its Board sync off or stopped, writes nothing that reaches the Board, so the
   note was untrue while the fleet is mixed. The owner's courier result now carries
   `origin_chat_link: "owner_written"` (`kanban_origin_creation.origin_link_fields`) only when it holds
   the origin chat's unreleased `created` link and its sync is enabled and running. `await_task_id`
   hands the owner's result back through `result_out=`, `kanban_placement.owner_chat_link` turns it
   into `placed.chat_link`, and the board-delivery note reads only that. No answer yet (a queued
   request) or an older owner falls back to `queued_local`.
2. Same change: the owner's actual decision is returned, so a `local-<sha256>` chat an ancestor's
   `created` link proves (`proven_foreign_chats`) now gets `owner_written` instead of `queued_local`.
3. `_link_origin` keeps skipping every chat on the owner's gateway, whatever its profile, now
   documented with the reason: the owner's reconcile is that chat's gateway and releases on its next
   pass any `created` row of it that it does not derive itself (a courier card has no
   `creator_chats_resolved` event). Measured with the (gateway, profile) comparison: the link was
   written, then `{'released': 1}` on the next reconcile. The hub subscription still reaches that chat.
   A test pins the skip.
